#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0258 expect=skipped domain=ADAE
#note "AE block WITHOUT the AESEQ column (STUDYID, DOMAIN, USUBJID only). The retired guard var_exists(AE.AESEQ) made this a silent clean EXECUTION; since the D110f/D118 rewrite onto AE._matched_ the same presence test is a DECLARATION -- Requirements.Variables.All [AE.AESEQ] -- so the missing column SKIPS the rule with a reason (D89b: declare => skip). This scenario is the pin on that delta: it is the one case where the flag rewrite changed an outcome, and it changed it from unreportable to reported."
#library standard=adamig version=1-1
dataset ADAE
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AESEQ   type=Num
col AEDECOD type=Char
---
S1 | 001 | 1 | HEADACHE
S1 | 001 | 2 | NAUSEA
S2 | 001 | 1 | RASH
---

dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
---
S1 | AE | 001
